# Sprint 1 Report
Video Link:
## What's New (User Facing)
* We can log in to Homestr via the WebUI, although secure login is not yet implemented,
  just dummy login.
* The WebUI dashboard has been built out. It currently shows live online/offline status,
  and has controls for things like adjusting light levels and colors. Controls for
  smart speaker volume and playback is also there. None of it is functional yet,
  because we have not implemented the APIs and actually integrated devices. Changes also
  should appear live in all open browser windows.
* Device registration has also been implemented. Admins can add and remove devices, while
  regular users can only control them. Devices persist across restarts.
## Work Summary (Developer Facing)
We developed the schema first with UML diagrams, and started planning the app with User
Stories. Then we designed the schema for the database, and we started writing out the design
of our program, including tools, codinge style, and the description of our UML design into
text to our CLAUDE.md file. We wrote our domain model into domain-model.md and our database
scheme into an init.sql file. In the CLAUDE.md we explained the general system overview,
including a breif description of the frontend, backend, and persistence implementations.
We also included a description of our spec driven development desired workflow. We included
our desired directory structure for the program. We also described how we wanted the program
to build using docker. We also included our desired coding conventions for C++ and Typescript.
And finally our aomain archetechture translated from our UML diagrams into text.

This was all done before implementing any AI or agentic coding, except for some usage for
research and troubleshooting on which tools to use to build the program. After that was all
written we asked Claude the familiarize itself with our documentation and spot any
potential roadblocks or inconsistencies before we started building anything. It suggested
some small things like a few changes to our database schema that may have caused issues down
the line, and we discussed these live over a Discord video call and decided which direction
to go and had it make those changes to the CLAUDE.md file. Then we asked it to start
scaffolding the project using our documentation and specs. Eventually we started adding
fature implementations to a Roadmap.md file in the docs so that we could track implemented
features vs yet to implement ones. Once we had a rough version of the project built
we started implementing the ability to build the project via docker. As of now the project
should build on any system with docker and be usable with dummy test devices in the WebUI.
